WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.131
(Are you awake yet?)
[MAYBE IT’S STILL TOO EARLY.]

00:00:10.131 --> 00:00:10.410
[MAYBE IT’S STILL TOO EARLY.]

00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:13.127
You’re playing tough scenes today.

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:14.281
Yes.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.877
- I have to cry in the morning, afternoon…
- And we have this.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.019
You play the father.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.450
[MAYBE THAT’S TOO MUCH.]

00:00:26.213 --> 00:00:27.450
(They’re like real siblings.)
[ALWAYS FIGHTING.]

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.681
Stop acting childish, Bonnie.

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:31.680
Save our audience from a headache.

00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:34.102
They can tell. They see the truth.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.109
What truth?

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.130
[BRIEFING TO ENSURE A COMMON UNDERSTANDING.]

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.010
[WHAT’S IN YOUR EYE?]

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.490
[AFTER THE ‘CUT,’ HIS CRUELTY DISAPPEARS.]

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.210
[HOW LOVEY-DOVEY.]

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.928
You’ve decided to turn around and walk away.

00:01:09.041 --> 00:01:11.038
(Kawi, you can go home.)

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.117
I’m... I’m feeling sad here.

00:01:17.395 --> 00:01:18.851
I can’t hold back.

00:01:19.339 --> 00:01:20.337
I want to stay.

00:01:20.482 --> 00:01:22.050
(Should I tell P’Fon to give you more scenes?)

00:01:22.297 --> 00:01:23.974
We can do more scenes on another day.
[YOU JUST DON’T WANT TO TROUBLE THE CREW, RIGHT?]

00:01:23.974 --> 00:01:25.250
[YOU JUST DON’T WANT TO TROUBLE THE CREW, RIGHT?]

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.090
[ARRANGING THE BLANKET.]

00:01:35.746 --> 00:01:36.327
Cut.

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.964
(Did we get it all?)

00:01:41.102 --> 00:01:42.268
(Help the girls, please.)
[SAVE THE GIRLS.]

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:42.810
[SAVE THE GIRLS.]

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.250
[THIS IS WHAT A JEALOUS GIRL LOOKS LIKE.]

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.610
[LET'S TAKE SOME PHOTOS.]

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:54.232
My eyes hurt.

00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:55.238
(That almost made you go blind.)

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.419
(She said her eyes hurt
because of your camera flash.)

00:01:58.635 --> 00:01:59.337
What?

00:01:59.814 --> 00:02:00.420
Really?

00:02:01.349 --> 00:02:03.136
If the picture turns out good,
I’m not sending it to her.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.690
[OH! SHE’S SULKING NOW.]

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:06.794
What’s it made of?

00:02:07.235 --> 00:02:07.899
(Just plain water.)

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.850
[LET’S CHANGE THE DRINK.]

00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:12.798
We’ve got it, P’Yo.

00:02:14.013 --> 00:02:14.857
Down the hatch.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.764
[FINALLY, THEY’VE GOT THE RIGHT DRINK.]

00:02:16.764 --> 00:02:17.970
Bottoms up.
[FINALLY, THEY’VE GOT THE RIGHT DRINK.]

00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:19.468
Let’s change it.

00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:25.103
Don’t drink it with this in it.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.601
That’d look funny. It’ll look unnatural.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:28.770
[IT’LL LOOK UNNATURAL.]

00:02:28.965 --> 00:02:29.724
(Is it water in there?)

00:02:33.788 --> 00:02:34.734
(Did it taste good?)

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.011
(She did her best to make it for you.)

00:02:37.914 --> 00:02:38.862
It’s really good.

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:41.165
P’View, you’re awesome. It’s so tasty.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.960
It’s just water with salt.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.930
[OOPS. YOU’VE BEEN CAUGHT.]

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:56.905
One, two, three.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.010
[TIME FOR SOME STILL SHOTS.]

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.090
[ADJUSTING TO FIND THE BEST POSITION.]

00:03:10.727 --> 00:03:13.567
(Left hand off the counter.)

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:13.810
[THEY GOT IT!]

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.810
(Try placing it somewhere else.)
[THEY GOT IT!]

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.730
[THIS WATERMELON IS SUPER SWEET.]

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.211
Why is mine so small?

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.570
[SWEETNESS OVERLOAD.]

00:03:39.394 --> 00:03:39.942
Bye.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.370
[SHOWING THE GIRLS HOW TO PLAY IT.]

00:03:53.128 --> 00:03:54.394
(Are you guys ready?)

00:03:54.394 --> 00:03:56.410
[GET READY TO SHOOT, LADIES.]

00:03:56.465 --> 00:03:57.620
My gosh.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.050
[DOKRAK’S STOMACH IS RUMBLING SO LOUD.]

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:08.499
The pain is gone.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.890
[YOU GUYS MUST GET IT DONE THIS TIME.]

00:04:21.743 --> 00:04:23.632
(Can you control the sound of your stomach?)

00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:25.712
Yes. P’Eed handled it.

00:04:26.748 --> 00:04:27.678
(Handled it how?)

00:04:27.841 --> 00:04:29.197
He said, “Don’t make a sound.”

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.487
How did it sound?

00:04:31.487 --> 00:04:31.960
[DIDN’T KNOW STOMACH SOUNDS COULD BE TAMED.]

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:32.802
I didn’t hear it.
[DIDN’T KNOW STOMACH SOUNDS COULD BE TAMED.]

00:04:32.802 --> 00:04:33.770
[DIDN’T KNOW STOMACH SOUNDS COULD BE TAMED.]

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.730
[REHEARSING.]

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.410
[FINDING A BEAUTIFUL POSE FOR THEM.]

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.890
[HUGGING EACH OTHER SO TIGHT.]

00:05:04.075 --> 00:05:05.694
Then you lie down. The end.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.050
[P’FON IS ALSO HELPING
ADJUST THEIR SITTING POSITION.]

00:05:12.682 --> 00:05:16.065
Look at each other for a bit.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.900
You go, “My breath stinks.”
[WATCHING THE DEMO FIRST.]

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.223
“I haven’t brushed my teeth.”
[WATCHING THE DEMO FIRST.]

00:05:19.616 --> 00:05:20.311
Something like that.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.914
Turn around, guys.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.130
[THEY LEAVE VERY QUICKLY.]

00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:30.736
My breath stinks too.

00:05:33.598 --> 00:05:34.303
No!

00:05:35.245 --> 00:05:36.171
Your breath doesn’t stink.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.850
[SHOWING THEIR SWEETNESS
THIS EARLY IN THE MORNING.]

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.250
[LET’S GO BRUSH OUR TEETH.]

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:56.200
SATURDAYS AT 8:30 P.M. ON GMM25

